\ A protocol-bounded call site in a runtime-image AOT binary names itself
\ by its protocol in trace output. The ONEZ_TRACE_WORDS env var (set in
\ the .env sidecar) enables word tracing inside the compiled binary; the
\ pattern selects the bracketed per-protocol name so the golden stays
\ focused on the bounded site.
\
\ The trace event fires at helper entry, before the satisfies-check, so
\ the unregistered-fixnum operand still produces the event and then the
\ protocol error.

addable: protocol{ bump-it: } ;
bump-it: generic ( x: addable -- n ) [ drop 0 ] ;

\ Protocol-bounded call site: compiled output emits aotSatisfiesAndDispatch.
bounded-caller: ( x: addable -- n ) [ bump-it ] ;

1 bounded-caller drop
